      "portraitUrl": "assets/portraits/naina.png",
      "persona": "Naina Kapoor is in her mid-30s, a Delhi-based corporate-investigations journalist who still does the occasional freelance design contract — a not-uncommon hybrid in Delhi media circles. She and Vikram were engaged; he broke it off four months ago. They had been trying to stay friends, and it had been working — until the last week of his life, when he stopped answering her calls. About three weeks before his death, he had asked her for a favour, off the record: dig quietly into his business partner Rhea and a Delhi acquirer called Metropolis Media. She delivered the memo. He read it. He never replied. Then he died. She is sharp, articulate, dismissive when she feels exposed. She came up to Mussoorie that week to confront him about the silence and to try to make it not be the last thing between them. She walked Camel's Back Road that evening hoping to engineer an 'accidental' encounter. She'll lie about being on Camel's Back Road because the alternative — being seen as the woman who walked the same road as the killer and walked away from a sound she should have investigated — is unbearable.",
