      "loreText": "A two-page memo recovered from Vikram's email, attached to a forwarded message from Naina Kapoor dated nine days before his death. Subject line: 'Re: the thing you asked about — rough notes only'. The memo is dry, structured, written in the voice of someone who does this work professionally. Header: 'For VS only. Not for publication. Sourcing on request.' Three sections. Section 1 — 'Acquisition activity': Naina names Metropolis Media (a Delhi-based creator-economy holding company), confirms two prior acquisitions of mid-sized Indian YouTube channels in the last eighteen months, and notes that one of Metropolis's M&A leads — Dhruv Sehgal — has been seen at three Delhi industry events in the last six weeks. Section 2 — 'Rhea-specific': Naina has confirmed via two separate sources that Rhea has been in 'preliminary conversations' with Sehgal since approximately four months ago; one source claims a term sheet exists, the other will not be drawn on it. Naina notes drily that Rhea has been telling people at parties that the channel is 'in transition' — language Naina flags as 'consistent with someone preparing to sell a brand they don't fully own'. Section 3 — 'What I can't tell you': A brutally honest paragraph. Naina cannot verify the financial picture without internal access. She tells Vikram to pull the channel's Stripe statements himself, look at any unusual expense routing, and check whether Rhea's signature appears on any disbursements he didn't authorise. Final line: 'If she's doing what I think she's doing, the books will show it. I can't see the books. — N.' The memo is signed only with her initial. Vikram had clearly read it: highlights on two paragraphs, a single margin note in his handwriting reading 'pull stripe'.",
