      "loreText": "Vikram's WhatsApp thread with Naina Kapoor, recovered from his iCloud backup. The thread covers the thirty days before his death and tells a small story on its own. The first two weeks are warm and ordinary — design feedback on a thumbnail, a back-and-forth about a chai shop they used to go to, Naina ribbing him about his beard in a recent video. Three weeks before his death, his tone shifts to business: 'naina — favour. you still doing the corporate stuff or just designing now? quietly — what do you know about a company called Metropolis Media. and rhea.' She replies within the hour: 'still doing it. give me a week.' Eight days later she sends the memo (see attached evidence). His reply: 'this is — yeah. thank you. drinks on me next time delhi.' That is his last message to her. From that point onward she sends seventeen more messages over the next nine days. The first three are professional follow-ups — does he want her to dig further on Sehgal, has he pulled the Stripe statements yet, does he need a forensic accountant referral. The next several drift toward the personal — 'you ok?', 'are you avoiding me or avoiding the work', 'pick up na'. The last four messages, all in the 48 hours before his death, are voice-call attempts with no text — twenty-three calls logged in total across the window. None answered. The thread ends mid-attempt. There is nothing in it suggesting Naina knew he was in physical danger. There is everything in it suggesting she knew something was wrong.",
