  "endgame": {
    "branchOn": "firstConfronted",
    "paths": [
      {
        "id": "bisht-first",
        "triggerSuspectId": "bisht",
        "scriptedSuspectLine": "I see what this looks like. But you have it backwards. Inspector Devraj has been extorting me for years. He discovered my father's history with the Thakurs and threatened to frame me for their deaths unless I kept paying him. The land, the payments to Anya — all of it has been him bleeding me dry. When Vikram started digging into the Thakur case, Devraj panicked, not me. He killed Vikram on his own. I had nothing to do with it.",
        "followUpSuspectId": "devraj",
        "followUpScriptedLine": "He's lying. He's lying. He planned all of it. The Thakurs — that was him. He hired the men. He paid me to make the file thin. Vikram — he called me that night and told me where to be. He told me to handle it. I was always just his weapon. Fifteen years of loyalty and he just threw me away."
      },
      {
        "id": "devraj-first",
        "triggerSuspectId": "devraj",
        "scriptedSuspectLine": "It wasn't my idea. None of it was ever my idea. Bisht made me do it. Fifteen years ago, the Thakurs — that was him. He paid me to bury the file. And Vikram — he called me that night and told me the boy knew everything. He told me to handle it. I'm just a constable who got in too deep.",
        "followUpSuspectId": "bisht",
        "followUpScriptedLine": "Devraj has been under extraordinary strain. I've tried to help him for years. If he has confessed to something terrible, I am of course shocked. But I had nothing to do with this."
      }
    ],
    "finalRevealNarration": [
      {
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "text": "The full picture comes into focus. Mr. Bisht is the mastermind. He ordered the deaths of the Thakur family in 2011 for revenge and profit. He ordered Vikram Singh's death this month to protect that secret. He never lifted a finger himself."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "text": "Inspector Devraj Khanna is his weapon. A sub-inspector who took a bribe in 2011. A full inspector who answered a phone call at 8:00 PM, drove to Camel's Back Road, struck Vikram with his service lathi, pushed him over a broken railing, and went back to the station to write a three-paragraph report. Fifteen years of being someone else's instrument."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "text": "Anya Devi is the fulcrum. She saw too much before the Thakur robbery, was silenced by school money for her son, and walked Camel's Back Road for two weeks as the Grey Lady — a mother trying and failing to find the words that would have saved Vikram's life. After he died, she wrote you the letter that brought you here."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "text": "Prof. Kabir Iyer wrote the second letter. He came to beg Vikram to bury his plagiarism, argued with him at the chai shop, and went home. When his conscience cracked, he nudged you toward the Thakurs."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "text": "Rhea Bhatia entered the cottage at 5 AM to wipe a memory card and hide an embezzlement that would have ended her career. She did not kill anyone. She tampered. She profited. She tried to inherit a brand."
      },
      {
        "speaker": "Narrator",
        "text": "Naina Kapoor walked the road that night, heard a sound she would replay for the rest of her life, and chose to walk away."
      }
    ]
  },

